{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef solve():\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    a = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    # Use BFS/DFS stack to generate all subset sums without recursion\n    n1 = n // 2\n    a1_set = set()\n    stack = [(0, 0)]  # (index, current sum)\n    while stack:\n        i, cur = stack.pop()\n        if i == n1:\n            a1_set.add(cur)\n        else:\n            # two possibilities: include a[i] (mod) or skip\n            stack.append((i+1, (cur + a[i]) % m))\n            stack.append((i+1, cur))\n    a1 = sorted(a1_set)\n    a2 = []\n    stack = [(n1, 0)]\n    while stack:\n        i, cur = stack.pop()\n        if i == n:\n            a2.append(cur)\n        else:\n            stack.append((i+1, (cur + a[i]) % m))\n            stack.append((i+1, cur))\n    ans = 0\n    import bisect\n    for x in a2:\n        j = bisect.bisect_left(a1, m - x)\n        if j > 0:\n            cand = a1[j-1] + x\n            if cand > ans:\n                ans = cand\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <utility>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid solve() {\n    int n;\n    long long m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        cin >> a[i];\n    }\n\n    int n1 = n / 2;\n    set<long long> a1_set;\n    vector<pair<int, long long>> stack;\n    stack.push_back({0, 0});\n    while (!stack.empty()) {\n        auto p = stack.back();\n        stack.pop_back();\n        int i = p.first;\n        long long cur = p.second;\n        if (i == n1) {\n            a1_set.insert(cur);\n        } else {\n            stack.push_back({i + 1, (cur + a[i]) % m});\n            stack.push_back({i + 1, cur});\n        }\n    }\n\n    vector<long long> a1(a1_set.begin(), a1_set.end());\n\n    vector<long long> a2;\n    stack.clear();\n    stack.push_back({n1, 0});\n    while (!stack.empty()) {\n        auto p = stack.back();\n        stack.pop_back();\n        int i = p.first;\n        long long cur = p.second;\n        if (i == n) {\n            a2.push_back(cur);\n        } else {\n            stack.push_back({i + 1, (cur + a[i]) % m});\n            stack.push_back({i + 1, cur});\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for (long long x : a2) {\n        auto it = lower_bound(a1.begin(), a1.end(), m - x);\n        if (it != a1.begin()) {\n            --it;\n            long long cand = *it + x;\n            if (cand > ans) {\n                ans = cand;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    solve();\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.3378546504536644e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0004391897819004953, -0.0002727136597968638, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.000433112756581977, -1.0132738680113107e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.072883037